{"body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nA backend repeating itself does not establish parity with ptrace, and a later retry must not erase an earlier divergence. This change retains candidate verification, reference verification, and the cross-backend comparison as separate observations, bound to the selected validation plan and the exact test and cell artifacts. The scorecard reports matches, failures, incomplete attempts, and never-measured cells separately.\n\nTask: kvm-lane-to-full-determinism-and-parity\n\n## Evidence and activation\n\nThe shared typed verifier authenticates the retained plan, source identity, selected population, complete operand invocations and reports, output hashes and dispositions, and every recorded attempt. Current reports require complete output evidence; historical report formats retain their explicit compatibility path. Duplicate fields, contradictory summaries, missing producers, and missing selected comparisons cannot qualify as clean evidence. Retained imports preserve an earlier failure when a later attempt matches or produces no comparison.\n\nThis commit series supplies the cumulative schema 10 producer and reader support. The validation writer remains disabled and both existing backend-parity selectors still run ordinary verification. The parent reader must consume the landed shared types before the prepared writer and selector activation follow. An empty selected parity population reports zero measured parity, even when ordinary validation is complete. This support change adds no measured parity matches.\n\n## Determinism\n\nEach parity operand must first satisfy strict canonical ordinary verification, including nonzero INFO record counts, exact output identity, and no time or I/O-buffer relaxation. The cross-backend report retains its named structured Detcore comparison envelope; the independent all-records pilot remains a separate measurement with its original failures preserved. Neither comparison's result is substituted for the other.\n\nThe synchronous tracing initializer also calls the existing thread-number equalization helper used by the other tracing initializers. This restores their common root guest ID convention while preserving synchronous log-tail capture. The guest measurements below confirm root ID 3 for both operands.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nThe evidence model preserves exit status, signals, stdout/stderr hashes and byte counts, syscall values, virtual time, and retained comparison results. It does not count an unavailable comparison as a pass. The KVM readdir fixture additionally requires creation-order-independent enumeration for a small directory that fits in one getdents64 buffer. This series does not resolve the separate scheduler/join failure or group-cancellation ordering work.\n\n## Relationship to gVisor\n\nThe KVM operand is the Reverie KVM backend loading shared Detcore. No separate determinism implementation or launch-only substitute is introduced.\n\n## Validation\n\nAt support source `85dd5e5c`, checks passed all 162 named methods across canonical comparison, CLI log comparison, record envelopes, verify, tracing, and Detcore log comparison. Earlier affected-source checks passed 238 manifest-plan library tests and 34 harness tests. The actual scorecard and pressure self-tests passed concurrently in 292.364 and 112.999 seconds wall (373.244 and 71.016 aggregate CPU seconds); both clone-helper isolation checkpoints executed. These focused runs used a 16 GiB bound and do not certify the official 5 GiB gate.\n\nThree predeclared trials of the one readdir cell each produced a first cross-backend divergence and a retry divergence. Both backends independently passed strict verification, the small-directory assertion passed, and root IDs agreed at 3. Ptrace recorded ten RDTSC callbacks and KVM none. These are measured failures, preserved separately from the support checks; the change does not establish backend-wide parity.\n\nThe historical 5,760 cells and 9,413 observations survive byte-for-byte after lossless JSON compaction; only the top-level schema differs from main. Actual selected inventory is 756 cells, including three custom cells. Inventory is not execution evidence. The separate two-ID all-records pilot refused its output directory before any guest ran and adds no comparisons.\n\nAt the final support source `e8e5ed8ee5647c06d30f5453ee3251073dc849ed`, the four shared schema 10 controls passed and all 16 exported evidence fixtures remained byte-identical. The exact 97-candidate argument control and the distinct 756-cell timeout/population control each passed. Formatting and full workspace/all-targets Clippy with third-party backends and denied warnings passed; Clippy took 51.728 seconds wall and 101.893 aggregate CPU seconds. Its earlier oversized-enum failure is preserved; storing the same report in `Box` fixes the storage issue without suppressing the lint or changing the wire format.\n\nThe final app target compiled and its build-only Nextest inventory selected the intended arithmetic control. The published Hermit binary is SHA256 `77b75f844625ebb022bf3ec691967a1acf4dfb3f84aa9fbe8c0d91fcc13c460a`, built from the final support source. The subsequent counted app attempt exhausted its 22-CPU-second budget during runner preparation, before test execution; it is incomplete, not a pass. The previous preparation refusal is also retained. Completing that bounded control remains follow-up work; its CPUID and timeslice flags make it an output-report control, not unrestricted backend qualification.\n\nEarlier failed checks, including the initial pressure failure, remain recorded. Landing uses the owner's soft-green policy; no whole-validation-graph green receipt is claimed.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABSfosHg","author":{"login":"rrnewton"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"[impl agent, gpt-5.6-sol]\\n\\nRepair pass pushed at b1d18789dad31f310c8ff26360469e25f7d27ca4.\\n\\nThe exact head now:\\n- admits disabled probe rows only when they carry typed backend-parity evidence or the parity-specific no-result disposition;\\n- classifies a failed or divergent ptrace reference as incomplete-parity-evidence, with no candidate result or copied divergence coordinates;\\n- checks SaBRe path eligibility before cross-backend comparison;\\n- bounds and accounts retained-log normalization and cross-backend comparator CPU on success, refusal, and timeout;\\n- includes the full backend-parity report in evidence identity and rejects conflicting same-run receipts;\\n- requires compared_outputs on current matched/diverged verification reports;\\n- synchronizes pressure-test CellResult fixtures and tracked schema 8.\\n\\nExact-tree validation:\\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check\\n- cargo clippy -p hermit -p hermit-manifest-plan --all-targets -- -D warnings\\n- cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --lib: 154 passed\\n- cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --bin test-harness: 19 passed\\n- cargo test -p hermit --lib: 236 passed\\n- cargo test -p hermit --bin hermit: 220 passed\\n- ./ci/compat-envelope/scorecard.rs self-test-and-check: passed\\n- ./ci/compat-envelope/pressure-test.rs self-test: passed\\n\\nscripts/validate.rs --self-test reached its nested rebase-freshness refusal because this branch is one commit behind origin/main. It did not run the live validation DAG. No DAG, selected-cell population, SCORECARD.md, or cells.json observation content changed in this repair. This head now needs fresh independent adversarial review; I am the repair implementor and am not attesting it.","createdAt":"2026-09-04T05:23:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945#issuecomment-5536099358","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABSf3G4A","author":{"login":"rrnewton"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"[impl agent, gpt-5.6-sol]\n\nThird repair pushed at `e5ff17ecd0c5d758cd50a45ac0b52a6d0f3df71b`; fresh independent review requested.\n\nThe three remaining findings are addressed at production boundaries:\n\n1. SaBRe path eligibility is evaluated for every candidate terminal outcome before any ptrace reference launch. Ineligible matching and divergent candidates both become `incomplete-parity-evidence` / no-result, and neither starts ptrace. Controls also prove eligible SaBRe match and divergence retain their intended meanings.\n2. The scorecard self-test now invokes the actual `observe-results` and `import-results` commands in a clean clone. Each command admits and renders a valid tracked disabled KVM parity row while excluding an ordinary disabled row for the same coordinate.\n3. Production `run_cell_with_parity` controls drive ptrace reference divergence, crash, and wall-timeout. In every case the candidate attempt remains an intact canonical PASS, the outer cell is typed no-result, no candidate product failure or reference divergence coordinates escape, and the cross comparator does not run.\n\nExact-head validation:\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `cargo clippy -p hermit -p hermit-manifest-plan --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan` (157 library tests plus all binary/integration tests)\n- `cargo test -p hermit --lib` (236 passed)\n- `cargo test -p hermit --bin hermit` (220 passed)\n- `./ci/compat-envelope/scorecard.rs self-test-and-check`\n- `./ci/compat-envelope/pressure-test.rs self-test`\n\nNo DAG, selected population, generated scorecard data, or `cells.json` content changed in this repair. The existing landing dependency remains: PR #2944 and the single-DAG cutover first, then rebase and one activation in final `ci/dag/validate.json`.","createdAt":"2026-09-04T05:53:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945#issuecomment-5536335584","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABSf72ng","author":{"login":"rrnewton"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"[hermit2, mega-lander, unresolved, devbig014, role=reviewer]\n\nAdversarial exact-head review: **APPROVE**\n\nReview target: `rrnewton/hermit` `c5e6ec7b3ec0f97104c18ae14301d84377cb3c11..e5ff17ecd0c5d758cd50a45ac0b52a6d0f3df71b`\n\nFindings: none.\n\nI rechecked the original six findings and the three second-review residuals through the production boundaries:\n\n- disabled KVM parity evidence is admitted through both `observe-results` and `import-results`, while an ordinary disabled row at the same coordinate remains excluded;\n- ptrace-reference divergence, crash, and wall timeout retain the candidate attempt but yield outer `ERROR` / `no_result` with `incomplete-parity-evidence`, clear outer divergence coordinates, and never invoke the cross-backend comparator;\n- SaBRe path eligibility is checked for candidate matches and divergences before any ptrace reference launch; ineligible paths cannot become product results;\n- ptrace normalization and the cross-backend comparator share the cell wall/CPU bounds, retain measured CPU on timeout/failure, and participate in aggregate accounting;\n- the complete typed `backend_parity` report participates in evidence identity, so conflicting same-run receipts are refused;\n- current matched/diverged verification reports require `compared_outputs`, and parity binds the selected operand to those exact disposition/stdout/stderr hashes.\n\nGoalpost-moving assessment:\n\n- Assertions weakened: no.\n- Tolerance widened, exemption added, case skipped, or comparator relaxed: no. `CrossBackendDetcoreV1` excludes backend launcher/transport records only; it retains complete structured Detcore INFO payloads (including virtual time and RCBs) and refuses empty, partial, filtered, or unstructured comparisons.\n- Failure renamed or relabelled as a pass: no. Incomplete reference/comparator evidence is typed `no_result`; a real cross-backend mismatch is `parity_failure`.\n- Check deleted instead of satisfied: no.\n\nPopulation/evidence audit: no DAG or manifest-selection files changed; `cells.json` changes only schema 7→8; existing retained observations are unchanged. The scorecard adds the parity view with all current pairs explicitly unmeasured, so no live parity evidence is manufactured.\n\nIndependent focused verification at the exact head:\n\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --lib parity -- --nocapture` — 6 passed\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --lib production_ptrace_reference_failures_preserve_the_candidate_as_no_result -- --nocapture` — 1 passed (diverge/crash/wall-timeout controls)\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --lib ptrace_golden_normalization_is_bounded_and_accounts_a_timeout -- --nocapture` — 1 passed\n- `cargo test -p hermit-manifest-plan --lib failed_backend_comparator_retains_its_cpu_measurement -- --nocapture` — 1 passed\n- `./ci/compat-envelope/scorecard.rs self-test-and-check` — passed, including `disabled-parity-front-doors`; tracked 5,744-cell population current\n- `git diff --check c5e6ec7b3ec0f97104c18ae14301d84377cb3c11..e5ff17ecd0c5d758cd50a45ac0b52a6d0f3df71b` — passed\n\nResidual limit: this is code/fixture validation; I did not claim a live KVM/DBT/SaBRe parity measurement. The patch correctly leaves those scorecard pairs unmeasured.\n\nVerdict: **APPROVE** for exact head `e5ff17ecd0c5d758cd50a45ac0b52a6d0f3df71b`. This comment is review evidence only; I did not apply an attestation/approval label.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:03:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945#issuecomment-5536413342","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABVCx59w","author":{"login":"rrnewton"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=reviewer]\n\nAPPROVED-AT: codex e8e5ed8ee5647c06d30f5453ee3251073dc849ed\n\nRelayed independent Codex-family adversarial review of the current source. The review extends the complete prior review through 85dd5e5c and independently verifies the four changed paths and every remaining tree entry. The reviewer made no product changes and ran no tests.\n\nThe implementation checks that were pending in the source report below have now run: four shared schema 10 controls passed, all 16 exported fixtures remained byte-identical, the distinct exact 97-candidate argument and 756-cell timeout/population controls each passed, formatting passed, and full workspace/all-targets Clippy with third-party backends and denied warnings passed. The normal push hook also accepted the default-feature warnings check. These are focused results, not a whole-DAG receipt or a backend parity qualification.\n\nThe source review preserved all earlier rejection controls: ordinary candidate/reference verification, complete output and invocation identity, exact retained attempt history, contradictory or duplicated data, missing selected comparisons, nonzero consumed records, and unavailable evidence. A retry cannot erase an earlier divergence. Producer and selector activation remain a separate follow-up after the parent reader consumes the landed shared types.\n\nIndependent report SHA256: 709c58364a7a1eab262d6eee9e9a84f462da993ee53330508ba4c380936e8125.\n\nAPPROVE the exact source at Hermit e8e5ed8ee5647c06d30f5453ee3251073dc849ed, tree 2a12bfa0a6a22dd036b781c6be1e46831025d885, based on main 765b07c26344fdd2aa198b687c6658fbe6fe3bf3. No source blocker found in this narrow addendum. The prior complete native/Codex review chain through 85dd5e5cb78a793f7ba2f9aeceb6914457e388bc remains applicable outside the four changed files. This approves source, not pending check results or cross-backend runtime parity.\n\nI read the complete boxed-report patch, the incoming main count correction, and the affected enum, constructors, validators, negative controls and population caller. The exact 85dd-to-e8e5 delta is 2,759 bytes, SHA256 89f6ff03db0118e67b01d8318359964464383d7b79037ffa669d37f7a740a686. It contains only:\n\n- ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger/schema10.rs: Completed.report becomes Box<BackendParityReport>, and the actual from_result_rows constructor uses Box::new(report).\n- ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger/schema10/tests.rs: the existing completed fixture boxes the same report. No fixture input or assertion changes.\n- ci/manifest-plan/src/runner.rs: a factual comment now describes the pinned selected population. The exact 97 total, KVM 75 / LiteInst 21 / SaBre 1 split, ptrace-reference presence, per-cell guest-argument equality and fatal readdir argument assertions are unchanged.\n- scripts/validate.rs: imports main's existing required-cell fixture count 734 to 756. The selected population and timeout computation are unchanged.\n\nBoxing changes storage, not the report's wire object. Serde still uses the same tagged enum/field and delegates the boxed value to the same BackendParityReport serializer/deserializer. BackendParityCellAttempt::verdicts still checks both ordinary matches, exact candidate/reference guest arguments, report.validate, and equality against each retained attempt report. Its existing mutable negative control still removes comparison input identities and requires refusal; field/method access dereferences the box. Complete attempts, unavailable reasons, recursive duplicate rejection, report hashes, outputs, comparator policy and the classification of retries are unchanged. No lint allowance or weakened validation was added.\n\nThe required population correction is supported independently by committed ci/expected-e2e-plan.json: 756 entries, 130,014 bytes, SHA256 6db8f539f9e5deaacb05e500f768ca1c77eceeae2eb2607e158950d3e1038e8a. That file is byte-identical at old main 1a5392a1753910ef7269434154cc46ce077019f3, incoming main 765b07c26344fdd2aa198b687c6658fbe6fe3bf3 and prior support 85dd. I inspected the real test's ManifestSet::select(Population::Required) caller and its unchanged exact selected readdir cell/budget assertions. This is correction of an obsolete expected count, not a selector change, range allowance or newly manufactured population. Running that existing test on the composed source remains a check, not a result inferred from JSON.\n\nIndependent whole-tree composition checks found exactly those four changed paths relative to 85dd. All 1,720 other entries preserve exact Git object identity/type/mode, including cells.json, the prior incoming-main dependency pins, selectors and disabled producer. The four final file hashes exactly match the independently prepared patch-plus-main union. All 41 original author-header/message byte pairs remain in order; there is one additional Box/comment commit. Total source entries remain 1,724. This does not use commit ancestry as a substitute for content equality.\n\nActual prior failure remains failed: native-43-clippy at 85dd exited 101 after 48.878881 seconds wall and 96.127821 CPU seconds. Its stderr reports only the large_enum_variant compilation error: Completed at least 3,032 bytes versus UnavailableWithReason at least 1,280 bytes; enum at least 3,040 bytes. The correction addresses Clippy's suggested indirection rather than suppressing its warning. Failure record SHA256 ec37d521c1d74fcb2fa232c57e05de7b54bafa550603de4eeb9849e78be67bd5; stderr SHA256 b1b107bf9e126f1b82e0c24d2da693c92c56bca62859bc68a4c84db988913396. The historical failed record and stderr were read directly, and no rerun success is invented.\n\nAlready-required checks still pending at this source review: the shared schema10 parser/negative controls and exported-fixture byte identity; the exact selected-count/timeout fixture; formatting; and the normal workspace/all-targets/third-party-backends Clippy command with -D warnings. Recovery owns their actual receipts. I ran no builds, tests or guests and added no whole-DAG receipt prerequisite. Previously recorded failed guest comparisons, closed-stdin loader failure and historical native failures retain their original source and status. The ordinary support approval does not enable the schema10 producer or qualify a failed KVM cross comparison.\n\nGoalpost-moving assessment: no assertion weakened; no tolerance widened, exemption added, case skipped or comparator relaxed; no failure relabelled as a pass; no check deleted. The count change replaces a demonstrably stale constant with the existing exact population and retains its equality assertion. The Box change preserves the same report value and all guards. No product/ref/index changes were performed by this reviewer.\n\nBinding: final-binding.json SHA256 eb24dbc56d8cd24d3b6aed28d98cf3977c5b3e56cd3073f49c88b3f2129c249a. Preparation SHA256 42960c84c1de3f3a2f8325a95542614d187ac4311082dda50e1043380ff44c74. The preparation bound the three-file boxed-report patch SHA256 2e3b125fa60372a776e0df9b85c330e7bcfa0e66d6e10ca958eebe7022649615 before the final head existed; this addendum binds the actual composed source.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-17T01:45:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945#issuecomment-5707168247","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"files":[{"path":"SCORECARD.md","additions":17,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/compat-envelope/cells.json","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/compat-envelope/pressure-test.rs","additions":7,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/compat-envelope/scorecard.rs","additions":2838,"deletions":185,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/dag/validate.json","additions":4,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/backend_parity.rs","additions":409,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/backend_parity_policy.rs","additions":54,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/bin/test-harness.rs","additions":428,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger.rs","additions":8,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger/schema10.rs","additions":1689,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/ledger/schema10/tests.rs","additions":684,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/lib.rs","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/runner.rs","additions":1323,"deletions":46,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/validation_dag.rs","additions":87,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"ci/manifest-plan/src/validation_dag_static.rs","additions":6,"deletions":6,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"detcore/src/logdiff.rs","additions":7,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/backends.rs","additions":14,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/logdiff.rs","additions":225,"deletions":135,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/record_envelope.rs","additions":50,"deletions":38,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/tracing.rs","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/verify.rs","additions":41,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/canonical_verdict.rs","additions":265,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/lib.rs","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/src/logdiff_report.rs","additions":238,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/tests/app_strict_verify.rs","additions":20,"deletions":5,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"hermit-cli/tests/verification_report_consumers.rs","additions":40,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/fixtures/README.md","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/fixtures/schema10-matched-cell.json","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/fixtures/schema10-matched-plan.json","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_artifacts.rs","additions":398,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_cell_results.rs","additions":267,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_classification.rs","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_evidence.rs","additions":418,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_history.rs","additions":34,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/lib/validate_test_results.rs","additions":771,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/validate.rs","additions":84,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tests/e2e/manifests/backend-parity-c.yaml","additions":2,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"headRefOid":"e8e5ed8ee5647c06d30f5453ee3251073dc849ed","mergeCommit":{"oid":"2a4142371e74aebea3cbd8b4c8329fc819d324f9"},"reviews":[],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[],"title":"Retain complete validation and backend parity evidence","url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945"}
